/-!
# The sporadic inspection in 15.3.42

The actual component quotient acts faithfully on every supplied model,
with its component exactly the preimage of the inner automorphisms.
The complete J₂ case constructs the compatible full-automorphism
identification: its two local candidates exclude equality of the ambient
quotient with the component, and the sharp outer bound finishes the action.

The full sieve still requires exclusions of M₁₁, M₁₂, M₂₂, M₂₃, M₂₄,
J₄, HS, He and Ru. J₃ is excluded by source 1.1.5(3f). No complete
sporadic-sieve or source-numbered 15.3.42 theorem is asserted here.

Source: Aschbacher--Smith, combined manuscript (1 March 2004),
1.1.5(3f), printed pp.501--503, and 15.3.41--42, printed p.1138.
-/
